---
// The client's Terms and Conditions, supplied 21 Oct 2026. Wording changes go
// back to the client rather than being made here.
//
// Changed from the supplied text on 21 Oct 2026, at the client's request: the
// opening no longer reads "trading as Pixel Surveys" after the ABN, and the
// contact email is the site's own inbox, CONTACT_EMAIL, not the contact@
// address the draft gave.
//
// No "Last updated" line: the client's text does not give a date for this
// one, and LegalPage leaves it out rather than showing an invented one. Pass
// updated="YYYY-MM-DD" once the client supplies it.
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  CONTACT_PHONE,
  CONTACT_PHONE_DIAL,
} from "../data/contact-info";
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms that apply to drone surveying, aerial imagery, mapping and spatial data services provided by Pixel Surveys."
>
  <h2>General</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms apply to services provided by Pixel Surveys
    ABN: 57 734 170 338, to the client. By accepting a quote in writing or
    instructing Pixel Surveys to proceed, the Client agrees to these Terms and
    to the scope, deliverables, fees and conditions in the accepted quote. Where
    a quote contains conditions differing from these Terms, the quote
    conditions apply to those services.
  </p>

  <h2>Services and scope of work</h2>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys provides drone surveying, aerial imagery, mapping, spatial
    data processing and related services as specified in the accepted quote,
    which outlines the scope, deliverables, formats, fees and estimated
    timeframes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Work outside that scope, including additional processing, revised
    deliverables or changed requirements, may incur additional fees and affect
    delivery dates, and will be agreed before proceeding. The Client must
    advise the intended use of the data, required coordinate system, datum,
    accuracy requirements and file formats before work begins.
  </p>

  <h2>Site access and client responsibilities</h2>
  <p>
    The Client must provide accurate project information, arrange agreed site
    access, and disclose relevant hazards, restrictions, site conditions and
    induction requirements before attendance. The Client is responsible for
    any landowner permissions or site access approvals allocated to them in the
    quote; Pixel Surveys arranges the operational approvals required for its
    drone operations.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where access is unavailable, conditions differ materially from those
    described, or work cannot proceed safely or lawfully, Pixel Surveys may
    postpone, modify or cancel the work, and additional costs may be charged
    where agreed or permitted under the booking terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Weather, safety and cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    Drone operations depend on suitable weather, visibility, airspace, site
    conditions and regulatory requirements. Pixel Surveys determines whether
    conditions are suitable for safe operations and acceptable data collection,
    and may reschedule or agree an alternative arrangement where weather,
    safety, airspace restrictions or circumstances beyond its reasonable
    control prevent work proceeding.
  </p>
  <p>
    Client cancellations or rescheduling may incur charges for work completed,
    preparation, travel, accommodation and other reasonable costs incurred.
    Applicable cancellation fees, notice periods and booking conditions are set
    out in the quote or booking confirmation before the Client commits.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Accuracy, quality and coverage depend on equipment, survey method, ground
    control, terrain, vegetation, weather and site conditions. The accuracy
    achieved is recorded in the delivery report issued with the deliverables,
    and that figure governs what the data may be relied upon for, in place of
    any figure published on the Pixel Surveys website or stated in general
    correspondence.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deliverables are supplied for the purpose agreed in the quote. Aerial
    imagery and photogrammetry represent visible surfaces; vegetation,
    buildings, water and other obstructions may prevent the underlying ground
    being measured directly, so some surfaces or elevations may be interpolated
    or less reliable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where the services rely on data supplied by the Client, including design
    surfaces, survey control or existing survey data, the Client warrants it is
    accurate, complete and correctly referenced to the stated coordinate system
    and datum. Pixel Surveys may rely on it without independent verification.
  </p>
  <p>
    These services do not constitute a cadastral or boundary survey and do not
    replace work that must legally be undertaken or certified by a registered
    surveyor. They are not a substitute for specialist engineering,
    geotechnical, environmental or other professional advice unless expressly
    included in the agreed scope. The Client is responsible for ensuring the
    deliverables suit their intended use and for obtaining any further survey
    or professional verification required.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Fees, payment dates and applicable expenses are set out in the quote or
    invoice. Unless otherwise agreed, invoices are payable within 14 days of
    issue. All fees are in Australian dollars, with GST shown separately where
    applicable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Additional expenses, including travel, accommodation, third-party data and
    approval fees, will be identified in the quote or agreed with the Client
    before being incurred, where practicable. Overdue payments may result in
    work being suspended or deliverables withheld until outstanding amounts are
    paid, subject to applicable law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where the services relate to construction work, claims for payment may be
    made under the Building and Construction Industry Security of Payment Act
    2009 (SA), and nothing in these Terms limits either party's rights under
    that Act.
  </p>

  <h2>Deliverables and intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Unless otherwise agreed in writing, Pixel Surveys retains intellectual
    property rights in its pre-existing materials, methods, workflows,
    templates and processing techniques. Once full payment is received, the
    Client is granted a licence to use the supplied deliverables for the
    project and purpose specified in the accepted quote; use for other
    projects, resale or broader redistribution may require written permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deliverables are provided in the agreed formats and coordinate system, and
    additional conversions, revisions or reprocessing outside the original
    scope may incur additional fees. The Client is responsible for retaining
    copies of delivered files, and any ongoing hosting, viewer access or
    long-term storage is subject to the arrangements in the quote.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys takes reasonable steps to protect confidential project
    information and handles personal information in accordance with applicable
    privacy obligations and the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">Pixel Surveys Privacy Policy</a>. Aerial data
    collection may incidentally capture people, vehicles, buildings or
    adjoining properties, and such information is handled accordingly.
    Information may be disclosed where necessary to deliver the services, to
    authorised project participants, or where required by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unless the Client advises otherwise in writing, Pixel Surveys may identify
    the Client as a client and use project imagery and data in its portfolio,
    website and marketing materials. Confidential
    information, pricing and commercially sensitive detail will not be
    disclosed, and individuals and adjoining private property will be
    de-identified where reasonably practicable.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability and client use</h2>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys performs its services with reasonable care and skill. The
    Client is responsible for providing accurate information and for decisions
    made using the deliverables, including ensuring they are appropriate for
    the intended purpose, and must notify Pixel Surveys in writing of any
    defect within 6 months of delivery.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys is not responsible for errors arising from inaccurate or
    incomplete information supplied by the Client, unauthorised alterations to
    deliverables, or use outside the agreed scope or stated limitations, to the
    extent permitted by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, Pixel Surveys' total liability arising from
    or in connection with the services, however arising, is limited to the
    fees paid for those services. Pixel Surveys is not liable for indirect or
    consequential loss, including loss of profits, revenue, production,
    contract, goodwill or data, delay or rework costs, or the cost of material
    moved or not moved.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these Terms excludes or restricts any consumer guarantee, right
    or remedy that cannot legally be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law
    or other applicable legislation. Where liability for breach of such a
    guarantee cannot be excluded, it is limited to re-supplying the affected
    services or paying the reasonable cost of having them re-supplied.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pixel Surveys holds Public Liability and Professional Indemnity insurance.
    Certificates of currency are available on request.
  </p>

  <h2>Delays, suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>
    Estimated timeframes may be affected by weather, site access, approvals,
    equipment issues or other circumstances beyond reasonable control, and
    Pixel Surveys will communicate material delays where practicable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate where the other materially breaches the
    agreement and fails to remedy it within a reasonable period after written
    notice. Pixel Surveys may suspend or discontinue work where payment remains
    overdue, necessary instructions or access are not provided, or continuing
    would be unsafe or unlawful. The Client remains responsible for fees for
    work completed and agreed costs incurred up to termination.
  </p>

  <h2>Disputes and general</h2>
  <p>
    Both parties will make reasonable efforts to resolve disputes through
    discussion and good-faith negotiation. Where a dispute is not resolved
    within a reasonable period, either party may refer it to mediation by a
    single mediator with costs shared equally, the mediator nominated by the
    Resolution Institute if the parties cannot agree. This does not prevent
    either party seeking urgent relief or exercising rights under applicable
    legislation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Amendments to the agreed scope or these Terms must be recorded in writing.
    If any provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to
    apply to the extent permitted by law. These Terms are governed by the laws
    of South Australia, subject to applicable Australian law.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="contact-block">
    Pixel Surveys<br />
    Email:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${CONTACT_PHONE_DIAL}`}>{CONTACT_PHONE}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
